// The Hard Knockback, found 2026-09-07. A fighter sent flying by a Full Power
// Smash enters state 213 (or 214 / 223), and FUN_001E9590 counts a phase timer
// at fighter+0x3D8 down once a tick from a value chosen per move - 50 for the
// D5 smash, 15 for D6, 32 for DF. Those are 30Hz frame counts, so at 60fps the
// victim leaves the constant-speed launch and drops into the gravity tumble in
// half its real time: measured, state 213 ended at tick 52 in BOTH arms, which
// is 104 vsyncs at 30fps and 52 at 60. The travel itself is already correct -
// the victim's position matched the 30fps arm to 0.15 units at the same real
// time - so only the duration is wrong, and doubling the three authored values
// restores it. The counter still decrements every tick, so unlike a parity gate
// this cannot leave a fighter stuck in the state.
[60FPS - knockback flight]
description=Double the launch-flight durations behind a Full Power Smash, so a knocked-away fighter stays airborne for its real-time span instead of half of it (FUN_001E9590). The three constants are dispatched on fighter+0x948, the STATE, not on a character or a move - every character launched into 213/214/223 is covered.
patch=1,EE,001E9614,word,2402001E // fighter STATE 214 launch: 15 -> 30 ticks
patch=1,EE,001E962C,word,24020064 // fighter STATE 213 launch: 50 -> 100 ticks
patch=1,EE,001E963C,word,24020040 // fighter STATE 223 launch: 32 -> 64 ticks

// The Lightning Attack, found 2026-09-07 - the Lightning Attack that follows a Full Power Smash.
// Four separate 30Hz frame counts and one lead prediction, all in the same
// chain, and every one of them has to be doubled or the Lightning Attack misses:
//
//   state 43  FUN_001F30E0  a 6-tick windup before the teleport fires
//   state 48  FUN_001F3668  the rise: (target - pos) * 0.25, added once a tick,
//                           exiting after exactly 4 ticks. Halving the step and
//                           doubling the count keeps the endpoint identical and
//                           doubles only the duration.
//   state 155 FUN_001E7408  after 20 ticks of diving, the horizontal speed is
//                           halved EVERY tick - the dive gives up. At 60fps
//                           that stall arrived before the dive could close.
//   FUN_001DE8A8            the intercept: target = foePos + foeVel * param_4,
//                           where foeVel is PER TICK and param_4 is a lead in
//                           TICKS. Measured at the call: the raw prediction was
//                           (87.5, -55.6, 40.0) from the foe at 30fps and
//                           exactly half that at 60, because the velocity is
//                           correctly halved while the tick count is not.
//
// The lead is doubled inside the solver rather than at the call site, because
// param_4 is built as fVar7 + 4.0 + fVar5 with a per-move fVar7 - doubling the
// literal 4.0 only corrects the move whose fVar7 is zero. FUN_001DE8A8 has
// exactly one caller, so changing the scale it uses touches nothing else.
[60FPS - pursuit timing]
description=Double the four frame counts and the intercept lead behind the Lightning Attack, so it connects at 60fps as it does at 30.
patch=1,EE,001F3194,word,28430008 // windup effect onset: 4 -> 8 ticks
patch=1,EE,001F31B0,word,2842000C // windup before the teleport: 6 -> 12 ticks
patch=1,EE,001F3754,word,3C013E00 // rise step 0.25 -> 0.125
patch=1,EE,001F3798,word,24030008 // rise length 4 -> 8 steps
patch=1,EE,001E769C,word,28430029 // dive stall after 20 -> 40 ticks
patch=1,EE,001DE918,word,4614A300 // lead x2: mov.s $f12,$f20 -> add.s $f12,$f20,$f20

// The camera, found 2026-09-08 - and it is one system, not a Cell problem. Every
// camera in the game is updated by FUN_001C69C8, which builds a target for this
// tick and then lerps the camera's euler angles toward it: cur += wrap(target -
// cur) * $f20. Both halves of that are per-tick and neither is compensated.
//
//   the chase   $f20 is the blend rate, 0.20 a tick, measured identical in both
//               arms. At 60fps it is applied twice as often, so the camera
//               converges in half the real time and then sits still.
//   the target  a scripted camera move counts fighter+0x558 down once a tick
//               from a length in fighter+0x55C that is authored in 30Hz frames
//               - 9 for Cell's Perfect Barrier, 30 for the move before it. The
//               progress the target is built from is 1 - remaining/total, so
//               the whole move plays in half its real time.
//
// Neither fix works alone: halving the blend alone leaves 12.84 degrees of mean
// orientation error against the 30fps camera and gating the move alone leaves
// 14.01, against 22.96 unpatched. Together they leave 1.52. That is the whole
// visible defect - the camera reaching its mark early and holding while the
// character is still animating - and it is fixed for every attack and every
// character at once, because both sites are shared by the entire game.
//
// $f20 is halved on the lerp path only, after the branch that chooses between
// lerping and snapping, so a scripted cut still snaps. It covers the look
// direction too, which is lerped with the same rate further down.
[60FPS - camera pacing]
description=Pace scripted camera moves and the camera blend by real time, not by tick.
patch=1,EE,000F1320,word,3C013F00 // 0.5f
patch=1,EE,000F1324,word,44810000 // $f0 = 0.5f
